{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The current best (config_010: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat, multiprofile; acc=0.6287) has established that avgpool+concat is the best aggregation/fusion pair and pca_n2000 is the best RNA encoder. However, the image encoder dimension is unexplored—only imagenet_vit_l has been tested. Config_002 changes only the image encoder to resnet50 while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (pca_n2000, avgpool, concat, multiprofile), making it a clean single-variable comparison to config_010. This will clarify whether a CNN backbone captures complementary spatial features that the ViT misses, or whether imagenet_vit_l is already near-optimal. Under the 4-experiment remaining budget, resolving the image encoder question is the highest-value uncertainty to reduce: if resnet50 helps, it opens a new exploitation path; if not, it confirms imagenet_vit_l and lets us focus remaining budget on finer-tuning other dimensions."
}

